SUMMARY:Inprint Claudia Rankine Reading
DTSTAMP:20260724T105421Z
DTSTART:20260914T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:General admission tickets will go on sale on Tuesday\, August 2
	5\, 2026 at 12 pm. \nClaudia Rankine will read from her new hybrid-genre w
	ork Triage\, followed by an on-stage conversation led by poet and Rice Uni
	versity professor Phillip Williams. The evening will conclude with a book 
	sale and signing. The event is presented as part of the 2026/2027 Inprint 
	Margarett Root Brown Reading Series.  \nWhether writing about intimacy or 
	alienation\, Claudia Rankine possesses a voice of unrelenting candor that 
	“shimmers with wisdom and fury” (The Telegraph). A MacArthur Fellow\, Rank
	ine is the author of five collections of poetry\, including her bestsellin
	g Citizen: An American Lyric\, which explores what it means to be an Ameri
	can citizen in a “post-racial” society. A defining text for our time\, Cit
	izen won the National Book Critics Circle Award\, the NAACP Image Award\, 
	the PEN Open Book Award\, and the Los Angeles Times Book Prize. She is als
	o the author of three plays\, including Provenance of Beauty: A South Bron
	x Travelogue\, which is performed on a bus ride through the Bronx\; and is
	 the editor of several anthologies\, including The Racial Imaginary: Write
	rs on Race in the Life of the Mind. \nRankine returns to Inprint with her 
	genre-defying new work Triage\, which collides the lyric with narrative\, 
	memoir\, image\, and essay to offer her most personal and emotionally reso
	nant writing yet. Triage follows the turbulent friendship between two char
	acters\, the narrator and the theorist\, self-identified sisters strugglin
	g to define their wounded histories and their shared but separate lives. A
	ccording to Jamaica Kincaid\, “Claudia Rankine’s remarkable\, outstanding 
	odyssey—an account of our present\, which is also our past\, which is alwa
	ys our future—is beautifully rendered in a kaleidoscope of images and sens
	ations. Triage is exquisite.” \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.org/event/inpri
	nt-claudia-rankine-reading-2/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-claudia-rankine-reading-2/
LOCATION:Brockman Hall for Opera\, Rice University\, Entrance #18 off Rice 
	Boulevard\, Houston\, TX\, 77005
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
