BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-w
 ebsite.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-website.jpg
UID:v4jD4_8PL3WF7sQvypV9V
SUMMARY:Inprint Cool Brains! Series presents Elizabeth Acevedo
DTSTAMP:20260724T105421Z
DTSTART:20261018T140000Z
DESCRIPTION:Free tickets will be available starting Monday\, September 14\,
	 2026. \n \n\nFree and open to the public\nFree copies of Anger Is Only a 
	Shadow for the first 100 families\nAppearance by celebrated Houston writer
	 Jasminne Mendez\nMeet the author followed by a book sale and signing\nBus
	 scholarships available for student groups – full scholarships for public 
	schools\, partial scholarships for private schools upon availability. For 
	information\, email info@inprint.org\n\nBooks available through Kindred St
	ories\n\n\nAnd more!\n\n\nThe 2026/2027 Inprint Cool Brains! Series proudl
	y presents National Book Award winner and renowned poet Elizabeth Acevedo\
	, sharing her new YA novel Anger Is Only a Shadow. \nKnown for YA novels f
	illed with poetry\, humor\, and heart\, Elizabeth Acevedo is the New York 
	Times-bestselling author of The Poet X\, which won the National Book Award
	 for Young People’s Literature\, the Michael L. Printz Award\, the Pura Be
	lpré Award\, the Carnegie medal\, the Boston Globe–Horn Book Award\, and t
	he Walter Award. She is also the author of With the Fire on High\, which w
	as named a best book of the year by the New York Public Library\, NPR\, Pu
	blishers Weekly\, and School Library Journal\; and Clap When You Land\, wh
	ich was a Boston Globe–Horn Book Honor book and a Kirkus finalist. Acevedo
	 is a National Poetry Slam Champion and served as the 2022 Young People’s 
	Poet Laureate. \n“An irresistible story of family connection\, resilience\
	, and loyalty” (Kirkus starred review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow is Acevedo
	’s powerful new YA novel in prose and poetry. Lil is anything but small. S
	he’s rebellious\, she’s loyal\; she’s figuring out what kind of good perso
	n she wants to be\, or if she wants to be a good person at all. But more t
	han anything? Lil wants to be free. When her instinct for freedom leads to
	 another stay in D.C. juvenile detention\, Lil knows she’s lucky to just b
	e on probation. But judgment\, guilt\, and an ankle monitor weigh heavily 
	on her\, and she can’t shake that pinned-down feeling. The only person who
	 might understand is her big brother\, Aldwin. Except he’s more distant no
	w than just the hundred miles from his college. As her court hearing ticks
	 closer\, a question looms over Lil as the missed phone calls and strange 
	texts from her brother pile up: will she stay put\, or put her future free
	dom on the line? “A striking and nuanced portrait of the realities of juve
	nile detention and mental illness” (Publisher’s Weekly starred review) and
	 “intensely genuine” (The Bulletin of the Center for Children’s Books star
	red review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow a white-knuckle journal to self-under
	standing and doing the right thing\, no matter the cost. \n\n\nhttps://inp
	rinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-elizabeth-aceved
	o/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-el
	izabeth-acevedo/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
